{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560642-adaptation-of-major-creation-suggested-by-my-player","id":1560642,"title":"Adaptation of Major creation suggested by my player","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-15T14:35:03-07:00","id":1560642,"title":"Adaptation of Major creation suggested by my player","content":"So, one of my players came to me with an adaptation of the ritual <i>Major Creation</i> (Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy, p. 94) for his character.<br /> <br /> I would like to have some opinions, any opinion is welcomed. Here's the text he submitted:<br /> <br /> [Ritual] Feed the Pyre (Level 3 Ritual)<br /> An Adaptation of Major Creation for the Path Lure of Flames<br /> <br /> Lore &amp; Flavour<br /> Normally, the Lure of Flames is restricted by the thaumaturge's ability to safely channel and contain thermal energy in the palm of their hand. The flame can only grow as large or burn as hot as the caster's immediate willpower can dictate, capping out at the size of a bonfire.<br /> <br /> However, by studying the structural sacrifices of Major Creation, certain Tremere\u2014particularly pyromancers and military sorcerers\u2014realized that physical mass could be traded for destructive yield. By sacrificing a piece of their own flesh, the caster feeds the flame a mystical accelerant made of concentrated vitae and bone.<br /> <br /> The ritual requires the caster to completely sever their own thumb. As the Lure of Flames is invoked, the severed digit does not drop to the floor; instead, it floats into the air, instantly charring into a white-hot ember before violently detonating. The flesh provides the raw, volatile mass needed to expand the fire far beyond its natural limits, transforming a localized spark into a catastrophic inferno.<br /> <br /> System<br /> To cast this ritual, the thaumaturge must sever their own thumb, requiring a successful Willpower roll (difficulty 7) or the expenditure of a Willpower point. The caster must also spend 3 additional blood points on top of the standard cost required to activate the Lure of Flames.<br /> <br /> Once the ritual is prepared, the player rolls Intelligence + Occult. The number of successes earned dictates a multiplier that simultaneously affects both the physical size and the destructive potency of the subsequent Lure of Flames power:<br /> <br /> Size Multiplier: The maximum volume of the created flame is multiplied by the number of successes. For example, if a thaumaturge manifests a Level 3 fire (Torch size) and achieved 3 successes on the ritual, the flame expands to three times that volume, easily engulfing an entire doorway, vehicle, or small room.<br /> <br /> Damage Potency: The raw intensity of the heat spikes. For every success scored on the ritual roll, add +1 die of Aggravated damage to the final damage pool of the chosen Lure of Flames power.<br /> <br /> The Restriction: The fundamental nature of the fire is still dictated by the specific level of Lure of Flames being cast (e.g., you cannot use a Level 1 candle-flame to melt through reinforced steel, but a Level 1 flame with 3 successes will become a massive, roaring torch-like fire that inflicts 4 dice of Aggravated damage instead of 1).<br /> <br /> The Backlash: Fire is a fickle element to bind with flesh. If the subsequent Lure of Flames activation roll results in a botch, the expanded inferno instantly collapses back onto the caster. The thaumaturge takes the full, amplified Aggravated damage of the spell and cannot use their own Thaumaturgical proficiency to mitigate or soak the heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T16:27:41-07:00","id":1560643,"title":"","content":"Is there anybody out there? (Imagine Pink Floyd lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T21:37:19-07:00","id":1560647,"title":"","content":"Me, coming back from my hiatus (slowly).<br /> <br /> The basic gist of it seems sound, learn as a ritual and make a sacrifice, empower Lure. It's also relevant that you can manage a similar result with guile alone, so the effect is less &quot;cause lots of damage&quot; and more &quot;access fuel more easily&quot;.<br /> <br /> All that considered, my points would be:<br /> <br /> 1. Have a comparison table on how to achieve a similar effect to any particular result with just common materials. This isn't strictly important but helps to keep a grounded perspective.<br /> <br /> 2. Major problem: it's uninspired. Just making the standard effect get bigger and badder isn't all that interesting even if balanced. I'd try to brainstorm some tangential benefits over nonmagically sacrificing a bottle of Molotov.<br /> <br /> 3. Possibly too strong: successes applying to two parameters at same time. It also reduces control, which is something I think a ritual should add, not subtract.<br /> <br /> 4. Possibly too weak: geometric size growth, it is fine at first success, then gives diminishing returns. Exponential or table would probably work better.<br /> <br /> 5. Heavy backlash: you're already self-inflicting damage, spending extra Blood, augmenting the damage. For this particular power the backlash damage is way worse than the potential benefit 9/10 times. Fun on paper, but your player will soon reduce or stop usage because it isn't worth it, if they even survive the first botch.<br /> <br /> My suggestions:<br /> <br /> - Add the use of someone else's flesh to make the cost an adaptive strategy.<br /> - Success = 2\u00d7 size, +1 dmg. After that, allocate extra successes to size **OR** dmg, with size doubling again or something.<br /> - Make a few extra effects to be &quot;purchased&quot; with successes, like shaping area or making it *not* dmg/ignite some things in the area.<br /> - Keep the backlash as either less dmg or, better yet, loss of control. R\u00f6tschreck can be a better option than dmg, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T23:35:58-07:00","id":1560650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All that considered, my points would be:<br /> <br /> 1. Have a comparison table on how to achieve a similar effect to any particular result with just common materials. This isn't strictly important but helps to keep a grounded perspective.<br /> <br /> 2. Major problem: it's uninspired. Just making the standard effect get bigger and badder isn't all that interesting even if balanced. I'd try to brainstorm some tangential benefits over nonmagically sacrificing a bottle of Molotov.<br /> <br /> 3. Possibly too strong: successes applying to two parameters at same time. It also reduces control, which is something I think a ritual should add, not subtract.<br /> <br /> 4. Possibly too weak: geometric size growth, it is fine at first success, then gives diminishing returns. Exponential or table would probably work better.<br /> <br /> 5. Heavy backlash: you're already self-inflicting damage, spending extra Blood, augmenting the damage. For this particular power the backlash damage is way worse than the potential benefit 9/10 times. Fun on paper, but your player will soon reduce or stop usage because it isn't worth it, if they even survive the first botch.<br /> <br /> My suggestions:<br /> <br /> - Add the use of someone else's flesh to make the cost an adaptive strategy.<br /> - Success = 2\u00d7 size, +1 dmg. After that, allocate extra successes to size **OR** dmg, with size doubling again or something.<br /> - Make a few extra effects to be &quot;purchased&quot; with successes, like shaping area or making it *not* dmg/ignite some things in the area.<br /> - Keep the backlash as either less dmg or, better yet, loss of control. R\u00f6tschreck can be a better option than dmg, too. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My firs reaction was that it was perhaps too poweerful for a level 3 ritual (even though that's the level of Major Creation and Major Creation has MANY useful applications as it's very powerful and versatile to be able to create really larger objects out of nowhere), but then I started to think that we can decide the level after creating it.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of being able to use other's flesh as well. So, the size x2 per success and +1 dmg at first and then adding the option to use further successes to either increase the size again (e.g. by doubling it again) or adding another +1 dmg. Your idea of being able to &quot;purchase&quot; other extra effects with successes is quite interesting, like being able to shape an area (perhaps the sizee of a door) where the flame doesn't affect or even giving some control over the flames after they started (perhaps, but not necessarily by keping concentrating). R\u00f6tschreck is interesting, but as one player once pointed out can sound a bit silly for a &quot;blood sorcerrer&quot; to be suddenly frightened by the flames he himself created (a problem that Vampire only solved with Koldunism), but on a botch I think it would make sense, but I assume I still prefer the idea of completelly losing control over the fire. I agree it's a bit uninspired, but can't blame him, because Major Creation from Blood Magic is basically even less so, as it's a very straightforward ritual with not so much flavour whatsover, even if it's interesting as it follows the very good directions of buffing path powers, something that was basically discarded later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T02:30:08-07:00","id":1560652,"title":"","content":"I'm note sure what you or the player wants here.<br /> <br /> I would prefer to keep the size of aggravated damage pools predictable and bounded so that Kindred cannot easily burn up in one or two turns.<br /> <br /> Less flamethrowers, not more.<br /> <br /> That is a personal preference, you may have different priorities.<br /> <br /> I've seen Lure of Flames being considered a weak or boring path, and I can understand that, but I think the issue there is not that it does to little damage but rather that pure damage isn't really what you want in WoD combat. The best powers for WoD fighting tend to be about controlling the situation, movement, stealth, strength, speed, grappling, sight. Damage doesn't matter if you can throw someone out of a window, stake them or avoid them entirely.<br /> <br /> So if the issue is your player wants lure of Flames to be better I don't think this rite solves that.<br /> <br /> If you are happy with the concept, a possible alternative to increasing the damage is increasing the difficulty to soak it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T09:24:43-07:00","id":1560654,"title":"","content":"He wants a ritual to enhance his Path and I'm definitely not against it <i>a priori</i>, as Lure of Flames is rather lackluster in terms of damage, but the difficult (e.g.to soak with Fortitude) you mention is perhaps the only thing it does good, as it's already 9. That's also something I think could be perhaps worked around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T13:21:33-07:00","id":1560655,"title":"","content":"Just as a point of personal experience, I'd recommend a flat damage increase instead of allowing to convert extra successes to additional damage. The latter can escalate pretty quickly, and Lure deals damage <i>per turn</i> unless the fire gets snuffed out somehow. Vampires without Fortitude can't even soak it - to me, the main utility of Lure is as a weapon of terror that takes a target out of a fight.<br /> <br /> Maybe make it a multi-level Ritual and tie the damage bonus to the level, or add something like &quot;Flames can not extinguished by mundane means for X rounds&quot; while keeping in mind how that would fry anything without Soak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T13:41:01-07:00","id":1560656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560642-adaptation-of-major-creation-suggested-by-my-player?p=1560655#post1560655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a point of personal experience, I'd recommend a flat damage increase instead of allowing to convert extra successes to additional damage. The latter can escalate pretty quickly, and Lure deals damage <i>per turn</i> unless the fire gets snuffed out somehow. Vampires without Fortitude can't even soak it - to me, the main utility of Lure is as a weapon of terror that takes a target out of a fight.<br /> <br /> Maybe make it a multi-level Ritual and tie the damage bonus to the level, or add something like &quot;Flames can not extinguished by mundane means for X rounds&quot; while keeping in mind how that would fry anything without Soak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, my first thought was that exactly, tie the bonus not to the roll, but to a level. Now that I think about it again, perhaps the damage cap being the level of Thaumaturgy or the caster would be fair. I had another idea about the whole concept that would be the caster &quot;giving a part of himself to feed the flames&quot;, like for instance, &quot;trading&quot; unsokable damage to himself to the size and damage of the flame, but that's a wild idea and I need to think carefully. What you guys think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T13:47:19-07:00","id":1560657,"title":"","content":"One of the concepts I like about tying it somehow to the level is because unfortunatelly in the RAW for the game we don't make any clear distinction of the caster from the powers of a path in general, so that it even reminds me of Ur-Shulgi character's sheet, where in his paths it's written &quot;godlike proficiency in the ancients paths&quot; or something along these lines, but in RAW there's absolutely no distinction between Ur-Shulgi using &quot;Lure of Flames&quot; or &quot;Tom, the average pyromancer wannabe&quot; or &quot;average Joe wants to burn some things tonight&quot;. This is something V5 did really well with those blood potency bonus, that I really wanted to be able to somehow adapt to V20, but still haven't had the inspiration to. So, the way to make a difference is in the knowledge of rituals to augment such paths that sometimes (that more often than not) are kind of lackluster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T16:03:36-07:00","id":1560659,"title":"","content":"It seems okay but boring. I've never been a fan of things like, &quot;This Ritual just makes X power stronger and lets it deal more damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd prefer it to instead adds effects where the fire also burns the individual's soul (dealing Willpower damage), or increases the difficulty to resist Rotschreck, or the burns from the fire can't be healed for X number of weeks, or something along those lines rather than just being bigger damage or area or effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T18:38:22-07:00","id":1560662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560642-adaptation-of-major-creation-suggested-by-my-player?p=1560659#post1560659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems okay but boring. I've never been a fan of things like, &quot;This Ritual just makes X power stronger and lets it deal more damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd prefer it to instead adds effects where the fire also burns the individual's soul (dealing Willpower damage), or increases the difficulty to resist Rotschreck, or the burns from the fire can't be healed for X number of weeks, or something along those lines rather than just being bigger damage or area or effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it's boring, as is <i>Major Creation</i> itself. That's why I'm trying to come up with something more unique, but even though your idea is interesting (burning the individual's soul), it makes the ritual incrediblly more powerful, so then it would definitely need to be of higher level. I'm trying to keep it at most a level 5 ritual. The ideas suggestd by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> are cool because it makes it more interesting and also unique, like being able to exert some control over the flames, for instance or keeping &quot;area x&quot; away from the fire, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T19:32:07-07:00","id":1560664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560642-adaptation-of-major-creation-suggested-by-my-player?p=1560652#post1560652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm note sure what you or the player wants here.<br /> <br /> I would prefer to keep the size of aggravated damage pools predictable and bounded so that Kindred cannot easily burn up in one or two turns.<br /> <br /> Less flamethrowers, not more.<br /> <br /> That is a personal preference, you may have different priorities.<br /> <br /> I've seen Lure of Flames being considered a weak or boring path, and I can understand that, but I think the issue there is not that it does to little damage but rather that pure damage isn't really what you want in WoD combat. The best powers for WoD fighting tend to be about controlling the situation, movement, stealth, strength, speed, grappling, sight. Damage doesn't matter if you can throw someone out of a window, stake them or avoid them entirely.<br /> <br /> So if the issue is your player wants lure of Flames to be better I don't think this rite solves that.<br /> <br /> If you are happy with the concept, a possible alternative to increasing the damage is increasing the difficulty to soak it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem of Lure of Flames is that the utility of a power doesn't really come so much from what it can do, but from how hard it is to get a similar result without it. And with fire the answer is usually &quot;not hard at all&quot;, as you don't need much to get your hands on several liters of fuel and a match.<br /> <br /> Other than that, burning a Kindred (or anyone) to a crisp in a few rounds is kind of the actual idea. For me, &quot;balancing&quot; combat in VtM by keeping dmg bounded is kind of missing the point.<br /> <br /> What balances fire is:<br /> <br /> 1. it is a known factor. Vampires prepare against fire as they know it is a problem. They expect fire to be a default option whenever anyone wants a Kindred dead. Mitigation options abound because fire is a common problem and tool for everyone, everywhere.<br /> <br /> 2. It's easy to get out of hand, and magical fire is no exception. Causing destruction and mayhem with fire is easy, the hard part is not regretting the collateral damage. 9/10 times you want to harm someone, you don't want to burn everything around them to the ground, and the other 1/10 you can just use lots of gasoline.<br /> <br /> 3. It's inherently unsubtle, and this is big. If you use fire for any purpose, you'll probably leave very clear signs that you did so. In a game of secrets, conspiracies and manipulation, what signs you leave behind you is way more important than how efficiently you directly kill a target. A vampire that abuses magical fire will become known for that way too fast and dealt with accordingly as a safety liability.<br /> <br /> For bounding damage, that's something VtM is bad at doing to begin with, so I see as kind of a loosing battle. Better to adapt the setting to a system that actually handles combat well, which is something I think people avoid too much out of prejudice.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a> I think scaling the damage with the sacrifice is nice. More fine control, a clear price, keep it under control by circumstances rather than luck (as a good roll can throw any attempt at balance out the window).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry too much, but isn't a bad idea at all anyway.<br /> <br /> Another idea for optional effect is to draw inspiration from hidden fires and slow reactions: you could have something that ignites with a delay, or that burns slowly but steadily, less impressive at first but way harder to put down.<br /> <br /> Think batteries that explode in flames hours or days after the damage that caused the problem, forest fires that restart suddenly after quenched because some trees keep burning in the inside quietly for weeks, or coal mines that turn into persistent, evolving infernos for decades, hidding below ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}